// dag/test/fixture/endpoint_authority/api.dag — THE PROVIDING MODULE for the imported-endpoint
// controls in `test.claim.service_endpoint_supply_emit_control`. This is the shape the corpus
// actually writes: the host a service names lives in ANOTHER module and arrives through a by-name
// `import` (`extdeps.github.gists` declares `endpoint: default_api_base` while the datum lives in
// `extdeps.github.github`). A consumer imports ONE of these data declarations by name; the other is
// deliberately left unimported, so a control can demand that a name no import of the consumer lists
// does NOT answer -- scope is what the author wrote, not what happens to exist in the tree.
module test.fixture.endpoint_authority.api

data default_api_base: String = "https://api.github.com"

data unimported_api_base: String = "https://never.imported.example"
